---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { emailText } from '../data/site';
---

{/* Draft notice, for Matthew's approval. */}
<Base
  title="Privacy · Dr Matthew Hooton"
  description="What the forms on drmatthewhooton.com collect, why, who processes it, and how to ask about your data."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="block">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This notice explains what this website collects and what happens to it. Dr Matthew
          Hooton is responsible for any personal data collected through the site.
        </p>

        <h2>No cookies or analytics</h2>
        <p>This site sets no cookies. It runs no analytics and no other tracking.</p>

        <h2>The forms</h2>
        <p>
          The contact form collects your name, your email address and your message. The mentorship
          form also asks for your student's school year, your country or time zone, their coding
          experience, how you heard about the course, and anything else you choose to tell me.
        </p>
        <p>
          I use these details only to reply to you and, for a mentorship enquiry, to arrange a
          conversation. I do not share them with anyone else or use them for marketing. The legal
          basis is my legitimate interest in replying to messages sent to me, and, for a mentorship
          enquiry, the steps you have asked me to take before any agreement.
        </p>
        <p>
          The forms are run by Formspree, Inc., a company based in the United States. Formspree
          receives what you submit, stores it on its servers and delivers it to my email. Its
          <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> explains how it
          handles data.
        </p>
        <p>
          I keep messages for as long as they are useful for replying to you and, if your student
          takes the course, for running it.
        </p>

        <h2>Videos</h2>
        <p>
          The Mentorship and Research pages show videos from YouTube in its privacy-enhanced mode.
          In this mode, YouTube says that watching a video here does not change what you see on
          YouTube. When the video player loads, your browser connects to YouTube, which may store
          information in your browser under
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub logs visitors' IP addresses for security, as
          its <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">privacy statement</a>
          describes.
        </p>

        <h2>Your data</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask me what I hold about you, ask me to correct it, or ask me to delete it. Email
          me at {emailText}. If you are unhappy with how I have handled your data, you can complain
          to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
